<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Siebe downgraded at Lehman.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Siebe downgraded at Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siebe Plc was cut to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; at Lehman Brothers, a research note from analyst Chris Heminway at the brokerage said on Monday.</p>
<p>Hemingway said the stock had completed a re-rating procress and was trading in line with other premium-growth engineers.</p>
<p>He set a price target of 1,125p for the stock in 1997, which he said gave a return in line with the overall UK equity market.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
